      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "A residential roof replacement in Utah typically takes 1 to 3 days of active installation time, though the entire project from initial scheduling to final cleanup usually spans 1 to 2 weeks.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "1 to 3 days"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Active Installation Timeline (1\u20133 Days)"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "1 to 2 Days: Standard for a small-to-average home with a simple roof shape, a single layer of shingles, and no underlying structural damage."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "2 to 3 Days: Required for larger homes, steep pitches, complex rooflines (multiple dormers or valleys), or heavy tile/metal materials.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Total Project Timeline (1\u20132 Weeks)"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Pre-Production (3\u20137 Days): This includes the initial inspection, signing the contract, ordering materials, and securing any local city or county permits required in Utah.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              1
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Tear-Off & Replacement (1\u20133 Days): Removing the old roofing materials, inspecting and repairing the wood decking underneath, and installing the new underlayment and shingles.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0,
              2
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Weather & Seasonality: Utah\u2019s unpredictable mountain weather, heavy winter snow, or sudden spring/summer storms can occasionally cause brief scheduling delays. Spring and summer are peak working seasons, while late winter can sometimes offer more flexible contractor availability.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              3,
              4
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
